ng I needed to add was hot sauce to my yakamein because I wanted it a bit hotter. The crowd was an older crowd but it was good vibes. I enjoyed the music and the bartender was attentive even though she was really busy"},{"business_id":"faEtEyYmeiHZegXvRugl3w","review_id":"a2Y7JqXdnfW1pctE0zPbqQ","date":"2018-01-03T04:53:54","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9207748174667358,"text_excerpt":"I have been hearing about the bar with the best Yaka Mein for over 10 years now and I have finally had a chance to visit and it was well worth the price. This place is actually a bar with that serves food. The set up is small and it has a pool table and a D.J. and the drinks were very good. But what I came here for was the Yaka Mein, This was oh so delicious and I wish I could have it everyday on a cold Dallas Night (restaurant is in New Orleans). The soup had a perfect temp and flavor and the meat was real beef, not roast beef like other places use and real shrimp not those baby shrimp. And for an added bonus the basic plain naked wings were very good and I could have ate about 10 more a..."},{"business_id":"faEtEyYmeiHZegXvRugl3w","review_id":"8ZMh3zX8mrk8NdqTBjoUHg","date":"2019-02-22T20:30:10","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9133621454238892,"text_excerpt":"I only had the Yakamein (noodles, beef broth, beef, & shrimp) which was delish. I went during the day so it was mostly people coming in ordering food and leaving. You will not know this place sells food other than the sign outside. Menus provided at bar and you can place your order there as well."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
